{"parentUuid":"0e53c5d4-17e6-45b9-9134-44ca8700c407","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"c91673d1-a819-42dd-bc50-e22fc9ab14c8","agentId":"a3bb137d2ec9bec69","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013rwVE9XhRSiJf4YcgCBUYM","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tname: hq-work\n3\tdescription: 'Use when a human assigns you a GitHub issue (\"work on #N\" or \"/hq-work N\"). Takes it from claim to a reviewed PR.'\n4\t---\n5\t\n6\t# hq-work\n7\t\n8\t`N` = issue, `<you>` = `claude`, `codex` or `cursor`, `<PR>` = PR number. Windows: `hq.cmd` for `./hq`.\n9\t\n10\t1. Claim: `./hq claim N --agent <you>`. If it refuses, stop and tell the human why. Read what it\n11\t   prints: the issue, work in flight, overlapping files.\n12\t2. Context before code. Read only the docs the issue needs, then run\n13\t   `entire search \"<topic>\"`, `entire graph query \"<task>\"` and `entire brain brief \"<task>\"`.\n14\t   Before rewriting code you did not write: `entire why <file>:<line>`.\n15\t3. Plan inline in a few bullets. No spec or plan documents.\n16\t4. Build inside Scope, never in \"Do not touch\". Small commits, staged by name:\n17\t   `git add <file> <file> && git commit -m \"<what the product can now do>\"`.\n18\t   Push whenever you like: `git push -u origin HEAD`.\n19\t5. Verify: run the issue's Verify steps, then `./hq check` until it passes.\n20\t6. Sync with main. Not pushed yet: `git fetch origin && git rebase origin/main`. Already pushed:\n21\t   `git fetch origin && git merge origin/main` (never force-push). Fix conflicts in your own\n22\t   changes, `git add <files>`, then `git rebase --continue` or `git commit`. Re-run `./hq check`.\n23\t7. Write `.context/pr-N.md` (template below; `mkdir -p .context` if needed), then\n24\t   `./hq pr N --body-file .context/pr-N.md`. It pushes, opens the PR with `Closes #N` and sets\n25\t   `status:review`. Get the number: `gh pr view --json number,url`.\n26\t8. Trail: Entire opens a trail for your PR by itself. Check it with `entire trail show`, then run `entire trail ci-pr` (safe to re-run). Only if `trail show` finds none: `entire trail create --title \"<issue title> (#N)\" --type feature`.\n27\t9. Review, unless the issue is `size:S`: `entire review`. Fix real findings, commit, `git push`,\n28\t   re-run `./hq check`. Then `gh pr edit <PR> --add-label review:pass` and `entire trail ready`.\n29\t10. Report the PR link, check result and risks, then stop. Merge only on \"ship it\" (`/hq-ship`).\n30\t\n31\tPR body template for `.context/pr-N.md`:\n32\t\n33\t````markdown\n34\t## What changed\n35\t- <what the product can now do>\n36\t\n37\t## How verified\n38\t- <Verify steps you ran and what you saw>\n39\t```\n40\t<tail of ./hq check>\n41\t```\n42\t\n43\t## Risks\n44\t- <what could break, or \"none\">\n45\t\n46\t## Screenshots\n47\t<UI changes only, else \"n/a\">\n48\t````\n49\t\n50\tOut of scope: do not do it. Write `.context/new-issue.md` with the headings `### Goal`,\n51\t`### Acceptance criteria`, `### Scope`, `### Do not touch`, `### Blocked by`, `### Verify`,\n52\t`### Notes` (say \"Found while working on #N\" in Notes), then\n53\t`gh issue create --title \"<title>\" --body-file .context/new-issue.md --label status:needs-human`.\n54\tLink it on your issue: `gh issue comment N --body \"Follow-up: #M\"`. Carry on with your own scope.\n55\t\n56\tStuck (unclear criteria, waiting on another issue, a conflict in code you did not write):\n57\t`./hq release N --needs-human --note \"<one crisp question>\"`, then stop.\n58\t\n59\tDone means: every acceptance criterion met, `./hq check` passes with its tail in the PR, PR open\n60\twith evidence, `review:pass` (unless `size:S`).\n61\t"}]},"uuid":"73c3abf5-fdaf-46d8-9d87-5b7388f48bd4","timestamp":"2026-11-14T19:43:29.044Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0e53c5d4-17e6-45b9-9134-44ca8700c407","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"/Users/n